    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d243">

                <pb facs="0521" n="451" xml:id="pg451"/>

                <head>No. 243.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr. Lowell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-08-22"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 22,
                        1883</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 654.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your dispatch No. 591, of
                    the 20th ultimo, transmitting a copy of a communication from the agent and
                    consul-general of the British Government at Sofia, reporting his action in
                    endeavoring to secure an amicable settlement of the difficulties between the
                    American missionaries and the Bulgarian authorities at Sistova, I have to
                    request you to convey” to proper quarter the thanks of this Government for the
                    friendly and generous course of Her Majesty’s agent and consul-general at Sofia
                    in relation to this matter.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>ALVEY A. ADEE,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
